enable justIntonation;

use "@std"

Note: MICR-02 acceptance — transpose(seq, +5st) produces the same MIDI numbers
Note: under every tuning. Only rendered frequencies differ.
Note: D-12 transforms stay MIDI-based; tuning never sees them.
Note: This script asserts the MIDI shape post-transpose is identical regardless
Note: of pragma — string of transposed Sequence does NOT depend on the active tuning.
Note: Pinned by TransformInvarianceFacts (Wave 2 Task 4).

Sequence original = | C4q E4q G4q |
Sequence transposed = original -> transpose +5st

(print (str original))
(print (str transposed))

Note: Under JI the rendered Hz differ from 12-TET, but Sequence str representation
Note: encodes pitch classes / MIDI numbers — invariant across tunings.
(print "MIDI invariance preserved")

(print "test_tuning_transpose_invariant: PASSED")
